-- title:
--   Regularity of the special fibre at a good point
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a prime $q$ and a natural number $M'\neq 0$ the field $F=$ `fieldBar q M'` is the compositum over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, inside the Laurent series field $\bar{\mathbb Q}((t))$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ with $H=$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$.
--
--   **Base data.** A prime $q$ with $5\le q$, a level $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA` asserting `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, which by `hW` consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generic $j$-invariant lying in `ssJSet q`, the set of $j$-values all of whose elliptic curves have no nonzero $q$-torsion point. The hypothesis `hle` records the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$) into $F$.
--
--   **The constant reduction $R_0$.** A datum $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A (modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`, consisting of a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` from it onto the reduced function field with kernel its maximal ideal, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places, and the axioms that a constant lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when it lies in $A$, that `R₀.residue` induces the residue map of $A$ on constants, that every nonzero function can be scaled by a constant into `R₀.integers` with nonzero residue, that `R₀.placeMap` preserves degrees, and that it transports the divisor of a function with nonzero residue to the divisor of its residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Igusa and supersingular valuation rings.** An index $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$), a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $F$ indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$, and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of $F$ indexed by $W$, subject to: `hIg_inf`, which describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ at the distinguished line `lineInfty q` as the Gauss ring, namely $f\in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ iff there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((t))$; `hIg`, which for each line $\ell$ produces $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{red}_q(\gamma)\cdot\infty=\ell$ and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $\ell\mapsto O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$; and `hIg_perm`, which for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ gives a permutation $\sigma$ of the projective line with $(O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell))$ pulled back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equal to $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\sigma\ell)$.
--
--   For the supersingular family: `hSS_A`, that a constant from $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, which for $s\in W$ and $f\in$ `R₀.integers` whose order is non-negative at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which the order of the modular invariant $j$ (the image of `jq` under `coeffEmb`) is non-negative, and whose residue `R₀.residue f` lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, asserts both that the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and that for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `R₀.residue f`, the difference of that image and $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is carried to itself by pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t-a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there for every $a\in A$.
--
--   **The prolongation $R$.** A datum $R$ of type `RegularProlongation A F (xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2M') (levelH q M'))`, that is, a valuation subring `R.integers` of $F$ together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the reduced level-$q^2M'$ function field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing the residue map of $A$ on constants, with constants lying in `R.integers` exactly when they lie in $A$, and with every nonzero element scalable into `R.integers` with nonzero residue; `hR` identifies `R.integers` with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and `hR₀O` states that $f\in$ `R₀.integers` iff the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   **Constants and auxiliary data.** An element $\pi\in\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$. A subfield $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$ (`hκ`). A prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **The finite layer.** A finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ with $A_1=A\cap K_1$ (`hA₁`), which is a discrete valuation ring and henselian.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Equip $k_0$ with the algebra structure on $F$ obtained by composing $k_0\hookrightarrow\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $\bar{\mathbb Q}\to F$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ such that: the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $F$; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar{\mathbb Q}$ which is $K'$-linearly independent and every family $a$ of elements of the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i\,a_i=0$ forces $a_i=0$ for all $i$; and every element of $F$ whose Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb` belongs to $F_0$ —
--
--   then, writing $T_1$ for the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $K_1$, and given an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map sends $a\in A_1$ to the image of $a$ under $\bar{\mathbb Q}\to F$, and given $j_1\in T_1$ whose image in $F$ is the inclusion of the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` determined by `coeffEmb` applied to `jq`, with $j_1\neq0$, the following holds for the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X_1=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra `chartAlgFin` of elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf`, the elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, with `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A_1$.
--
--   The statement introduces the local abbreviations `InStalk`, `InMax`, `Centred`, `Reads` and `OffBranch`: `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` mapping to $x$ under `ιFin` there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h\notin y$ and $f\cdot h=g$ in $T_1$, and likewise on the infinite chart; `InMax x f` requires the same with the additional condition $g\in y$; `Centred P x`, for a place $P$ of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, says that $P$ is rational and that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and satisfies $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ less than $1$ iff `InMax x f`; `Reads x Q`, for a place $Q$ of the reduced level-$q^2M'$ function field, says that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in `R.integers`, with `R.residue f` in the valuation subring of $Q$ and in its nonunits exactly when `InMax x f`; `OffBranch x` says that for every line $\ell\neq\infty$ and every point $y$ of either chart over $x$ there is a chart element $b$ whose image in $F$ is a nonunit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which does not lie in $y$. Of these, only `GoodPt` occurs in the conclusion: `GoodPt x` asserts that `toBase` maps $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}A_1$; that $x$ specialises only to itself; that for every point $y$ of $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` over $x$ every chart element whose image in $F$ is a nonunit of `R.integers` lies in $y$, and likewise on the infinite chart; and that for every point $y$ of $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ does not lie in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7).
--
--   The assertion is then: for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ with `GoodPt x`, every $\varpi_1\in A_1$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_1$, and every element $\varpi_x$ of the stalk of $\mathfrak X_1$ at $x$ equal to the germ at $x$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi_1$ by the inverse of the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ isomorphism for $A_1$ followed by the global-sections map of `toBase`, the quotient $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X_1,x}/(\varpi_x)$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the regularity of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of the level-$q^2M'$ modular curve over the henselian discrete valuation ring $A_1$, at a closed point of the special fibre lying on the $\infty$-Igusa branch and over a non-supersingular $j$-invariant. It packages, in the frame of the Igusa base model, the ordinary-chart and cuspidal regularity results, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_reads_of_reads_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.eq_of_reads_of_reads_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.offBranch_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.offBranch_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel).
